msgstr ""
"`开始阅读全书 <read-cover_>`_ `下载精排 PDF 全书 <book-pdf_>`_ `探索全部 40 项管制点 <read-"
"atlas_>`_ `官方审批流程与通讯录 <read-contacts_>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:23 ../../site/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"A border barrier holds up computer parts and technical plans while two "
"research teams try to work together."
msgstr "两支研究团队试图合作，边境障碍却阻滞了计算机部件和技术图纸的流动。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:30
msgid "From an Open Republic of Ideas to a Guarded Horizon"
msgstr "从思想的开放共和国到设防的地平线"

#: ../../site/index.rst:33
msgid ""
"An open model can let a university, a small business or a language project "
"adapt a shared tool. These possibilities do not guarantee safety or equal "
"access. Our argument is that broad restrictions can damage cooperation even "
"when each country hopes to gain an advantage."
msgstr "开放模型可能帮助大学、小企业和语言项目，却不保证安全或平等。即使各方都想占优，广泛限制仍可能伤害合作。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:35
msgid ""
"Open AI also needs physical computers. Large training runs can require "
"advanced chips, memory and networks; smaller models can run on more ordinary"
" equipment. Controls on hardware and design knowledge can affect access even"
" when a model has a permissive license."
msgstr "开放AI需要实体电脑。大训练可能需要先进硬件，小模型可用普通设备；宽松版权许可并未消除硬件管制的影响。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:39 ../../site/index.rst:44
msgid ""
"Open models depend on chips, memory and computing infrastructure. A "
"restriction on one part can affect access to the whole system."
msgstr "开放模型依赖芯片、存储与算力设施。限制一部分可能影响整体可用性。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Hardware:** US rules cover specified chips and manufacturing items. China "
"proposes controls on specified processor and memory designs and certain "
"technologies for clusters with more than 10,000 cards. The scope depends on "
"the precise item and conditions. `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_"
msgstr ""
" **硬件：**  美国覆盖指定芯片及制造物项，中国提议指定设计和超万卡集群技术；范围取决于具体对象和条件。 `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:49
msgid ""
"**Models:** Chinese temporary registration has started, while new catalogue "
"prohibitions and restrictions remain proposed. US model-weight text and its "
"announced non-enforcement policy are separate questions. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_ `GAO26 "
"<https://www.gao.gov/products/b-337935>`_"
msgstr ""
" **模型：**  中国登记已启动，新增类别仍是草案；美国规则文本及不执行政策分别看待。 `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_ `GAO26 "
"<https://www.gao.gov/products/b-337935>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:51
msgid "The Fortress Trap: How Both Sides Can Lose"
msgstr "堡垒陷阱：双方如何一起受损"

#: ../../site/index.rst:54
msgid ""
"Imagine two research teams starting from one public AI model. A's team makes"
" it run with less memory. B's team tests errors and helps fix them. Sharing "
"the next improvements helps both, but each government worries about giving "
"the other a one-sided advantage."
msgstr "设想两队从一个公开模型出发。A降低内存需求，B发现错误并协助修复。交换下一轮改进对双方都有帮助，但各政府都担心单方面给对方优势。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:56
msgid ""
"We give the four endings invented preference scores: mutual sharing gives 17"
" each; withholding while the other shares gives 20 to the withholding "
"country and 3 to the sharing country; mutual restriction gives 5 each. "
"Higher means preferred within this example. The book explains why we assume "
"that ranking before showing how it creates the trap."
msgstr ""
"我们给四种结局设定虚构偏好分：相互共享各17分；自己保留而对方共享时，保留方得20、共享方得3；相互限制各5分。越高表示本例中越偏好。书中先解释为什么假设这种排序，再说明陷阱如何产生。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:58 ../../site/index.rst:63
msgid ""
"Two teams finish a computer by sharing parts and knowledge, then struggle "
"when a wall separates them. This illustrates the assumed game, not a "
"measured outcome."
msgstr "两队共享部件和知识时能完成计算机，被墙隔开后却难以完成。这是书中假设博弈的示意，不是实测结果。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:67
msgid ""
"A chooses a row and B a column. Both sharing gives 17 each. A alone sharing "
"gives A 3 and B 20. B alone sharing gives A 20 and B 3. Both restricting "
"gives 5 each. All scores are assumptions."
msgstr "A选行，B选列。双方共享各17分；只有A共享时A得3、B得20；只有B共享时A得20、B得3；双方限制各5分。所有得分都是假设。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:67
msgid ""
"#import \"figures/diagrams.typ\": game-theory-matrix\n"
"#game-theory-matrix(lang: \"en\")"
msgstr ""
"#import \"figures/diagrams.typ\": game-theory-matrix\n"
"#game-theory-matrix(lang: \"zh_CN\")"

#: ../../site/index.rst:67
msgid ""
"Four endings for the two teams. The scores are invented preferences; higher "
"means preferred within this example."
msgstr "两队的四种结局。分数是虚构偏好，本例中越高表示越偏好。"

#: ../../site/index.rst:74
msgid ""
"Each government then sees a reason to restrict: 20 beats 17 if the other "
"shares, and 5 beats 3 if the other restricts. Both choose walls and get 5 "
"each, although both prefer mutual sharing at 17 each. This is a possible "
"failure of cooperation under our assumptions, not a measurement of US or "
"Chinese policy. `GAME <https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~rafael/networks-"
"html/chapter1.html>`_"
msgstr ""
"各政府都看到限制的理由：对方共享时20优于17，对方限制时5优于3。双方筑墙各得5，却都更愿意合作各得17。这是假设条件下可能的合作失败，不是对中美政策的实测。"
" `GAME <https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~rafael/networks-html/chapter1.html>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:76
msgid "`Read the worked story and its limits <read-game_>`_"
msgstr "`阅读完整故事及其局限 <read-game_>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:78
msgid ""
"The legal records and research references distinguish what is already "
"operating, what remains proposed, and what is our analysis. They support "
"three practical reading habits:"
msgstr "法律及研究来源区分现行措施、提案和分析，支持三个阅读习惯："

#: ../../site/index.rst:80
msgid ""
"**Distinguish public files from first releases.** Existing public "
"technology, private derivatives and new open-source exports can take "
"different routes. A copyright license is not a government permit. `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"
msgstr ""
" **区分已有公开与首次发布。**  公共文件、私有衍生物及新开源出口路径可能不同。版权许可不是政府许可。 `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:81
msgid ""
"**Keep current registration separate from the draft.** China has begun "
"temporary registration for covered transfers; new prohibitions and "
"facilitated licensing remain proposals. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CNQA "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcjd/art/2026/art_b11d5c1e9374421e93e85dc87eba6e38.html>`_"
msgstr ""
" **区分登记与草案。**  临时登记已启动，新增禁止和便利许可仍拟议。 `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CNQA "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcjd/art/2026/art_b11d5c1e9374421e93e85dc87eba6e38.html>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Read deadlines in their proper scope.** The standard licensing clocks do "
"not promise the total duration of a project or the future automatic-"
"licensing process. The book links the responsible authorities and their "
"source records. `CNTIER "
"<https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=898>`_ `CNMEAS "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/dl/file/20211203230621.pdf>`_"
msgstr ""
" **按适用范围读期限。**  不能当成项目总时长或未来自动许可承诺；书中提供主管机关及来源链接。 `CNTIER "
"<https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=898>`_ `CNMEAS "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/dl/file/20211203230621.pdf>`_"

